Problem on Averages-9 - Placement Exercise
NOTE: This kind of question is very common in campus placement ( TCS, Wipro, etc.) because it makes the use of average and some basic logic.

Problem:
The average marks obtained by 25 students in a class is 64. 
If the average marks of 15 students is 72, find the average marks obtained by the remaining 10 students.

Solution:
Note: Formula of Average = Sum of observations / No. of observations.
Sum of observations = Averages X No. of observations.

Total sum of marks of 25 students = 25 × 64 = 1600

Total sum of marks of 15 students = 15 × 72 = 1080

Now the remaining 10 students' total marks = Total sum of marks of 25 students - Total sum of marks of 15 students

Remaining 10 students' total marks = 1600 - 1080 = 520

Number of remaining students = 10

Average marks of remaining 10 students = 520 ÷ 10 = 52

Final Answer
👍 Average marks obtained by the remaining 10 students = 52
